{"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"TrackingPlans"}],"roleHeading":"Framework","externalID":"TrackingPlans","symbolKind":"module","role":"collection","title":"TrackingPlans"},"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A tracking plan is the contract between an app and whoever reads its events: dashboards, a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"warehouse, a collector, another platform’s client. Each event’s document gives its version,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"consent category, properties and their JSON types, which ones every payload holds, and which are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sensitive","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", in a form that needs no Swift to read. Committed beside the events, it puts every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"change to them in the pull request as a JSON diff. Its check says which changes break what has","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"already shipped: payloads from installed app versions that a validating collector would reject,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and stored records the app could no longer decode.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlan","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" turns events’ schemas into files: an index, "},{"code":"tracking-plan.json","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and for each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"event a JSON Schema (draft 2020-12) document and an example payload. The files are values, so the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"same schemas give the same bytes on every run and platform, ready to commit for the people and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tools outside the app."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Checking compares the plan the events make now with the committed one by what the files mean. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlanCheck","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" is a match, a plan that is only out of date, or one with a breaking"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"difference: a change that, at the same version, would leave a stored record or an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"already-released app’s payload unable to decode or validate. Each "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlanDifference","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" names"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the event, the property and the change, and says whether it is breaking."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Only code compiled against the app’s event types can read their schemas, so the app writes a small"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"executable of its own: a type that conforms to "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlanCommand"},{"type":"text","text":", marked "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@main"},{"type":"text","text":". It writes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the plan to a directory, or checks it with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"check"},{"type":"text","text":". To run the check from the app’s tests instead,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackingPlanTesting"},{"type":"text","text":". The schemas usually come from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Event"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventMacros"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The module is a product of its own that "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Traffluent"},{"type":"text","text":" leaves out."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import TrackingPlans","import Traffluent","","@Event(name: \"signed_up\")","struct SignedUp {","    var plan: String","}","","let plan = try TrackingPlan(schemas: [SignedUp.schema])","let check = plan.check(against: plan.files)  \/\/ .matches","let paths = plan.files.map(\\.path)","\/\/ [\"tracking-plan.json\", \"signed_up.v1.schema.json\", \"signed_up.v1.example.json\"]"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The guide ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/trackingplanworkflow"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"covers the executable, the command plugins and the test.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Making a plan","anchor":"Making-a-plan","identifiers":["doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlan","doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlan\/File","doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlanError"]},{"title":"Writing a plan","anchor":"Writing-a-plan","identifiers":["doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlan\/files","doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlan\/files(carryingForward:)","doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlan\/write(to:)","doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlanCommand"]},{"title":"Checking a plan","anchor":"Checking-a-plan","identifiers":["doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlan\/check(against:)","doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans\/TrackingPlan\/check(againstDirectory:)","doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/doc